    "output_tokens": 306
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 7,
   "response_text": "The datautil doesn't show the feature dimension. However, looking at the error and the code, the issue is clear:\n\n1. The config has `\"input_dim\": 1` which is incorrect\n2. The actual training data has 105 features (from the error: \"mat1 and mat2 shapes cannot be multiplied (256x105 and 1x64)\")\n3. The training script loads data that has 105 features but then applies the incorrect config value\n\nThe bug is that `input_dim` should NOT be in the config at all, OR it should be set to the correct value (105). Looking at the code logic at line 192-193:\n```python\ninput_dim = X_train.shape[1]  # This would be 105\ninput_dim = mcfg.get(\"input_dim\", input_dim)  # This overrides it to 1\n```\n\nThe fix is to remove `input_dim` from the model config OR set it to the actual feature dimension (105). However, since the case description mentions \"healthy range\" for validation accuracy and we're looking for configuration faults, the most likely scenario is that `input_dim` should be removed from the config entirely, allowing the code to auto-detect it from the data.\n\nLet me verify this is indeed the root cause by checking the resolved config:",
